\section{Scope}

This supplement contains the material intentionally removed from the
page-limited main paper. Part~I gives the complete reference configuration,
error-bound audit, spatial-narrowband condition, component ablation,
paired comparisons, robustness, generalization, scaling, cost, certificate
diagnostics, and external-benchmark tables. Part~II reports the $-15$ and
$-20$~dB threshold region, where Phase~I delay poles collapse. The proofs
of the three flagship theorems are in the main paper; Part~III collects the
auxiliary derivations they rest on or extend -- local identifiability, the
scope of the three projection roles, exact scale elimination, the
nested-component information order, and the
regularization compatibility result -- together with the steps of the
flagship proofs that are routine rather than structural.

Abbreviations defined in the main paper retain their meanings. Throughout
this supplement, $P_{\rm cat}$ denotes the empirical catastrophic-event
rate, p95 and p99 the 95th and 99th percentiles, CI a confidence interval,
c-RMSE the inlier-conditional root-mean-square error, NMSE normalized
mean-square error, and RSS resident set size. Unqualified vector norms are
Euclidean, and unqualified matrix norms are spectral.

Every campaign statistic in Parts~I and~II comes from the frozen
\texttt{paper\_v4} campaign, under the within-suite paired protocol of the
main paper and the estimator constants of Section~\ref{sec:impl_supp}. Different suites use independent
seed roots and share no realization. Each accuracy cell contains $480$
trials unless a cost or C3 control is explicitly identified. The external
benchmark uses its own seed root and $960$ trials per cell, not
realizations shared with the independently seeded suites.
No estimator is tuned specifically for the supplement. Wherever a
supplementary figure extends a main-paper suite, it uses the
corresponding frozen campaign outputs and the same script as the
main-paper figures, with the SNR floor moved from $-10$ to $-20$~dB rather
than a separate experiment; independently seeded diagnostic suites are
identified explicitly where they appear.

\section*{Part I: Deferred Studies Inside the Operating Region}

\section{Reference Configuration and Error-Bound Audit}
\label{sec:reference_supp}

Table~\ref{tab:s_params} gives the configuration summarized in the main
paper. At the default UE position the minimum path-delay separation is
$3.28$~ns, marginally above $1/B_{\rm occ}=3.23$~ns, and the clock search
interval occupies $5\%$ of the $1/\Delta f=200$~ns unambiguous period.

