\emph{RIS element-phase calibration} (Fig.~\ref{fig:s_ris_calibration})
perturbs individual RIS phases at $0$~dB. The Phase-I-only median grows
from $6.58$~mm at zero error to $39.6$~mm at $10^\circ$ and $77.4$~mm at
$20^\circ$, where its catastrophic rate is $31.67\%$. The refined route's
curves show the corresponding improvement on the shared observations.
The oracle-calibrated median PEB remains near $0.124$~mm. The curves
quantify sensitivity to this perturbation, without attributing every
departure from the PEB to a single source of error.

