\section{Anatomy of the Algebraic CPD Read-Out Failure}
\label{sec:als}

The Algebraic CPD adaptation has $46.67\%$ catastrophic events at
$-10$~dB, $34.69\%$ at $0$~dB and $31.15\%$ at $30$~dB in the native
benchmark. Among failing trials, median position errors are $0.1802$,
$0.1794$ and $0.1797$~m at those SNRs, consistent with a persistent
factor-to-position mapping branch.

The factor-domain reconstruction remains accurate: at $0$~dB, failing
and successful trials have median observation NMSEs
$8.02\times10^{-4}$ and $8.00\times10^{-4}$; at $30$~dB both are about
$7.99\times10^{-7}$. All $448$, $333$, $303$ and $299$ failing trials at
$-10$, $0$, $10$ and $30$~dB report a unique three-panel assignment and
successful factor refinement. These fields support locating the loss
downstream of the factor fit. The behavior characterizes this
adaptation and mapping implementation, not the reference method
of~\cite{lin2021tensor} in general.

