\section{C3 Clock-Unit Control}
\label{sec:c3control_supp}

The control itself is Table~\ref{main-tab:c3_control} of the main paper:
Phase~II is isolated by giving all four routes the same $100$ MKSC-GI
initializers, so the routes differ only in how the clock coordinate is
carried. Three points about how it was run are recorded here.

The three CCOP parameterizations (seconds, nanoseconds and
$c_0\Delta t$) are separate arms with identical returned-candidate hashes.
This establishes implementation invariance for these tested arms;
mathematical profile invariance alone would not imply bit-identical
floating-point results.

The profiled route uses a median of $9$ outer evaluations, versus $13$,
$18$ and $13$ for explicit seconds, nanoseconds and distance units.
It performs $950$ certified clock solves in total. Position catastrophic
counts are $1$, $0$ and $1$ for the three explicit units, and $1$ for
CCOP-JVP; these small counts do not establish a general reliability
ordering. Each column's position and clock conditional RMSEs are both taken
over that route's non-catastrophic set, the trials triggering neither
catastrophic event.

