The accuracy and acquisition panels compare raw and compressed delay
estimation. The subspace diagnostics show compressed leakage and retained
energy; the latter approaches the white-noise reference $r/I=1/16$
below the operating region.}
\label{fig:s_compression}
\end{figure*}

\section{Receiver Modes Below the Region}

The receiver ordering persists below the operating region
(Fig.~\ref{fig:s_receiver}). At $-15$~dB, the scalar, dual-polarized
and full-EVS catastrophic rates are $43.75\%$, $10.63\%$ and $1.88\%$;
at $-20$~dB they are $85.83\%$, $31.67\%$ and $5.00\%$.
These end-to-end rates complement the local information and separability
results. Only $14.17\%$ of scalar trials remain position inliers at
$-20$~dB, so the reduced-mode conditional efficiencies rest on few trials.

