The linearization is accurate at every sample, the two columns agreeing to
between $9\times10^{-5}$ and $2\times10^{-2}$ in relative terms, so no
higher-order check is needed. The real Jacobian has rank $4$ and condition
number below $20$ at every sample, so the small bias is not the minimum-norm
solution of a rank-deficient system. Every zero-mismatch control returns the
true parameters to $2.6\times10^{-12}$~m and $2\times10^{-11}$~ps, nine orders
below the tightest accuracy scale compared against, and tightening the outer
tolerance by $10^{2}$ moves the reported bias by $5\times10^{-6}$~mm. All
clock certificates hold.

Position and clock behave differently. The position bias spans
0.0037--0.0804~mm, median 0.0186~mm, and stays at or below $0.18$ of the
sample's own PEB throughout, so it is not visible against the noise at the
low end of the evaluated range. The clock bias spans 0.19--5.38~ps, median
1.93~ps, and reaches $1.6$ times the sample's own CEB: at four of the nine
samples it is already comparable to or larger than the noise-limited clock
scale at $-10$~dB. Because the bias is deterministic while the bounds scale
with $\sigma$, both ratios grow as the SNR rises.

This is a local refinement diagnostic at nine samples. It does not exercise
Phase-I acquisition, and nothing here bounds the catastrophic rate or the
basin behaviour under spatial wideband.

\section{Retained-Polarization Weight}
\label{sec:alpha_supp}

The weight $\alpha_{\bS_{\rm mode}}=\|\bS_{\rm mode}\bTheta_k\bx_k\|^2/
\|\bTheta_k\bx_k\|^2$ of Theorem~\ref{main-thm:split}(i) quoted in the main
paper is computed directly, without synthesizing an observation or running an
estimator. It is a noiseless per-panel ratio in which the complex gain
$\beta_k$ scales numerator and denominator alike and cancels, and the
resolvability sweep fixes the Jones states of the two controlled paths
analytically from the overlap: $\gamma_{\rm ref}=\pi/2$ and
$\gamma_{\rm cmp}=\arcsin(\text{overlap})$ at $\eta=0$. Only $\bTheta_k$, the
two Jones vectors and the receiver mask are therefore needed. The separation
sweep moves the panels, so the geometry is rebuilt at every separation rather
than evaluated once at the default one.

